afety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written `work/supervisor.py`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json`. I expect almost no gain over the naive shield-only run, because nearly all the loss comes from the longer minimum green on through phases, which a supervisor can't shorten.\n\n**What it does:** it always returns a legal phase. When the network's pick is illegal, it takes the legal phase the network scores highest, not the shield's \"most halting vehicles\" phase. Otherwise the network decides, apart from two narrow tie-breaks.\n\n**When it overrides:**\n- **Only one phase legal:** during a minimum green, or with a single overdue phase, it returns that phase. The shield would give the same phase.\n- **Max wait coming:** if a phase would be forced at the next switch anyway, it serves it now. This needs a logit gap of at most 0.75 and a clear win on halting vehicles per second of green.\n- **Through vs left:** it prefers the left phase when the gap is at most 0.5, since a through green now blocks the junction for 20 s instead of 15 s.\n\nRaw disagreement with the network is 61%, almost all forced phases. The phase actually run changes in only 4 of the 4433 recorded decisions.\n\n**Checks:** replayed every recorded state one decision at a time (always legal), ran hand-made edge cases, and confirmed it uses only numpy and math. One-step replay can't show knock-on effects.\n\n**Predictions (veh-h):** low 36.1, nominal 47.0, high 57.85, about ±0.7 from seed noise.","ttft_ms":1093,"type":"result","duration_ms":766150,"uuid":"9f0c262f-b4a8-473e-9ea2-f18b64d25f79","ttft_stream_ms":949,"time_to_request_ms":73,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":27,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"mo